---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "UK Student Visa from Pakistan: CAS, Funds & Application",
  "description": "Prepare a UK Student application around official funding requirements, the CAS, visa fees, identity evidence and digital immigration status.",
  "intro": "Prepare a UK Student application around official funding requirements, the CAS, visa fees, identity evidence and digital immigration status.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "GOV.UK Student visa",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/student-visa"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student financial requirements",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/student-visa/money"
    },
    {
      "title": "UK eVisas",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/evisas"
    },
    {
      "title": "Faster-decision services",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/faster-decision-visa-settlement"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Choose the study route",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Student route is for eligible applicants aged 16 or over with a licensed sponsor, required English ability and sufficient funds. Applicants aged 16 or 17 need parental consent. From outside the UK, you can apply up to six months before the course starts."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Calculate the required funds",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Living costs are currently £1,529 per month in London or £1,171 outside London, for up to nine months, plus the course fees required on your CAS. Exceptions depend on your circumstances. Funds normally need to be held for 28 consecutive days, ending within 31 days of application.",
        "Build a funding worksheet from the unpaid CAS fees and relevant living-cost amount. Check account ownership, accessibility and statement dates against UKVI’s detailed guidance. An old PKR total cannot establish that the requirement is met."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Budget and submit",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The outside-UK application fee is £558. The healthcare surcharge is separate and depends on visa duration. Start through GOV.UK, follow the generated evidence and identity instructions, and keep the submitted form, receipts and document copies together."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Timing and faster services",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The usual outside-UK Student estimate is three weeks. Faster services depend on eligibility and availability. Priority usually means five working days for most eligible routes, not 24 hours; confirm the service offered during your application."
      ],
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "heading": "After the decision",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Follow the decision instructions for digital immigration status. Do not follow outdated promises of collecting a new BRP from a Post Office. Check your account and passport details before travel.",
        "Work and dependant rights depend on your permission and course. Graduate permission is two years for applications on or before 31 December 2026, changing to 18 months from 1 January 2027; doctoral graduates have a separate three-year provision."
      ],
      "source": 0
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
